so you've collected some full classified  sets some decent weapons and now you're  to optimize them to get the best out of  your build great but before you jump in  and spend all the division tech that  you've been saving up over the last few  weeks or months there's a few things you  should be aware of just sooo that you  can get the most bang for your buck to  fully understand what's being covered  we'll start by quickly going over gear  score in the early game from level 1 to  30 that's your character level that's  displayed and as your level increases  the level of gear and weapons that drop  increases too once you hit level 30 the  number displayed changes over to gear  score at the same time weapons and gear  that start to drop a now represented by  gear score as well the gear score  numbers are broken down into five tiers  these five tiers correspond to the world  tiers so will Tier one has 163 to 181  gear score items all the way out to  world tier 5 which has 256 to 286 or 293  for classified items excluding the  holster witches 295 and this is why most  will say just to rush up to world tier 5  as soon as you hit level 30  because gear found on the lower tiers  very quickly becomes obsolete as you  move through the world tiers the gear  score of an item reflects the quality of  the gear so in will tier 5 the gear  score of a standard item can range from  256 to 286 256 being the lower quality  and 286 being the maximum value that  piece of gear can be note gear score  does not take into account the talents  or stats that are on the weapon or gear  this and this is the reason to ignore  gear score at first and instead look at  the stats and talents and then worry  about whether it's worth the currency to  further optimize so a piece with 256  gear score but god roll talents will  always be more valuable than a piece  with higher gear score and rubbish  talents finally this may be obvious to a  lot of you but I've seen it asked a lot  if an item drops on a specific world  tier they can only ever have a gear  score within the range of that world  tier again I'll show this little chart  so a weapon that drops on world tier 4  can only be optimized to a maximum gear  score of 255 you cannot continue to  optimize it into the will tier 5 gear  score range  unless you're absolutely swimming in  division tic there's a few things you  can look at before optimizing your  builds recalibrate your gear before  optimizing if there are some stats to be  recalibrated do this before you start  optimizing optimizing a piece of gear  and then recalibrating a stat will be  undoing some of the optimization so for  example if you have a chest piece with  the rolls you're after that the main  stat is in the wrong area recalibrate  this before heading to the optimization  station or you'll be spending even more  division tick reoptimize in it  recalibrating isn't just useful to  change stats before optimization it can  also save you a bunch of diptych if you  bring your stats as close to the maximum  as possible before optimizing for  example if you have a classified hostel  with 1280 firearms 1380 stamina and  1,400 electronics and you've already  rolled the major stat into the state of  your choosing this piece is already  pretty close to being maxed apart from  the firearms but since you have an extra  slot you can recalibrate because it's a  classified piece if you recalibrated  firearms so that it was closer to the  maximum level it would mean that you're  spending even less on optimizing which  is considerably more expensive than  recalibrating the cost of using the  optimization station is two hundred and  fifty thousand credits and fifty  division tick per roll and it can take  up to 19 rolls to get to the maximum  gear score on an item costing a total of  four million seven hundred fifty  thousand credits and nine hundred and  fifty division tick now imagine that  over a whole six piece build and that  doesn't include weapons this is  obviously a worst case scenario because  you're feeling unlikely to get a piece  with the minimum possible stats that's  worth keeping let alone a whole build  but it gives you an idea of the  associated costs and how you should be  pretty happy with a piece before you  think about optimizing credits are  pretty easy to come by but how do you  increase your dev tech income right now  the single best way is to make sure that  you do your weekly and daily assignments  if all you do is complete them every day  and finish the weeklies you can earn a  total of a thousand of tech per week if  you have multiple characters you can  earn even more as the materials are  shared so with four characters you can  earn up to four thousand you can also  find a lot more division tech playing  resistance activities in the West Side  Pier farming the darks  extracting caches and exotic caches can  give a decent amount to but the  assignments are by far the easiest and  most time efficient way the optimization  station could be found down in the  terminal and at Camp Clinton I like to  start with weapons first particularly  the ones I use over multiple builds  careful not to get carried away though  if it doesn't have the perfect talents  save the diptych next onto the gear the  best piste without a doubt is the  holster as this increases all three main  stats after that look at what stats need  increasing maybe you need a little more  firearms to unlock that whip and talent  or maybe you have a piece that's really  lagging behind the rest when you're  optimizing your gear you'll notice that  it's the main step that takes the  longest to increase to maximum and this  is part of the reason that it's  recommended that you recalibrate these  first if possible the attribute that you  should put the lowest priority on is  armor the difference from the minimum  possible armor rolls to the maximum is  about 5% and with the way that armor  currently works in the game this equates  to about one bullet worth of mitigation  in fact the only reason to continue  optimizing until everything is maxed is  because your OCD is and like to see  everything completed like me but for the  rest of you mere mortals here is the  order that I'd recommend when you start  optimizing a belt when on a division  tech budget of course there are  exceptions to this but it's a good  starting point the max gear school you  can get on weapons and non-classified  gear is 286 and unclassified gear is 293  excluding the holster which maxes out at  about 295 the gear school given to your  agent is the average of all of your gear  so if your build is made up with a six  piece classified set everything is fully  optimized you'll have a gear score of  291 when getting the most out of your  gear versus the cost of optimization it  isn't about maxing out every piece of  your build it's more about focusing what  you need to work on first and where  possible recalibrate your gear as high  as you can before optimizing division  tech may be easy to get these days but  with proper planning you can save  thousands meaning you can optimize more  faster I feel like I may have missed an  obvious tip or two on the subject so if  you notice anything I may not have  covered let everyone know in the  comments below otherwise I must thank  Trigger 739 from the MG and discord  channel for the  your suggestion it's a true in-game  topic worth talking about in an area  where people often misuse their precious  division tech anyway thank you for  watching and I'll catch you in the next  one  Cheers  [Music]
 

